module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.gate_population_covers_only_new_subjects

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data gate_population_covers_only_new_subjects: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "gate_population_covers_only_new_subjects" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a gate whose population is NEW subjects, guarding a property that degrades in EXISTING ones** (INVALID STATE: a gate exists to stop a property of the standing corpus, and the population it actually ranges over is only identities enrolled in this change -- declared now minus declared at the resolved diff base -- so an already-enrolled subject that degrades into the same state passes unremarked.",

    "HARM: the gate reports coverage of a failure mode it only half covers, which is DESIGN section 4b rung inflation: an inflated class never ranks for climbing.",

    "SPECIMEN, confirmed by reading `v2.workflow.floor_enrolment_margin` rather than by the first recount of it. The module's own comment names the failure it exists to stop: a row measured at 450ms clears the ceiling on the run that measures it and is then a coin flip on every run after. THE GATED POPULATION paragraph then names, in terms, every newly enrolled test declaration -- `declared now` minus `declared at the resolved diff base` -- joined through `floor_run_base_test_decl_census`, and says a modified sibling whose name WAS at the lookup path is not enrolled. `enrolment_margin_blockers` folds that newly enrolled set; zero newly enrolled identities is the positive control. An ALREADY-ENROLLED row is therefore outside the gate by construction, and the comment says so: the gate closes that state for NEWLY ENROLLED identities only.",

    "THE SUBJECT ROW: `v2.test.claim.affected_set_universe.affected_set_universe_gate_processes_match_declared_gates` went from roughly 30ms to roughly 371ms on main and was never gated, because it was already enrolled.",

    "ARITHMETIC, because the first report of this specimen used the wrong quantity. The runner inflation envelope is MULTIPLICATIVE, not additive: 1.367x median and 1.653x p90 over rows with identical eval_steps (`floor_enrolment_margin_envelope_permille` is 1653, the p90). 302 is the DERIVED ENROLMENT BUDGET (`implied_clean_run_budget` of the 500ms ceiling over that p90), not the envelope. So 371 x 1.367 = 507, which is already over 500: the row crosses at the MEDIAN runner, not merely at p90. Do not restate this as 129ms of headroom against a 302ms envelope; that was additive arithmetic on the derived budget.",

    "WHY THIS IS NOT `check_subject_narrower_than_its_declared_claim`, which is the nearest neighbour and must not absorb this. There, an executing check is CITED for a population its implementation never names, so the narrowing is silent. HERE the gated population is declared honestly in the same module that states the purpose. The defect is the JOIN: a purpose sentence about a standing-corpus cliff, plus an increment-only range, is then read as coverage of the cliff. The inflation lives in that join, not in a hidden scanner. Widening the declaration to match the range (an honest repair of the neighbour) would make this gate stop claiming the 450ms coin-flip, and the standing corpus would remain unguarded -- which is this class still, only more honestly titled. The repair that climbs is ranging over the property's actual subjects, not renaming the increment gate.",

    "IT IS ALSO NOT `selection_view_read_as_population`: membership here is not a measurement threshold. It is a set difference over declared test declarations. The population is authored-stable and simply is not the standing set the purpose names.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: the new-enrolment path is mechanically preventable -- the module stamps itself DESIGN section 4b rung 2, and that stamp is honest FOR THAT POPULATION. The already-enrolled path has no executing wall for the same property. DESIGN section 4b(1) makes a class's rung the MINIMUM across its in-scope paths, so the failure mode the purpose sentence names -- a measured row that is a coin flip on the next runner -- sits at mitigatable for already-enrolled identities, and citing the gate's rung 2 as that class's rung is the inflation this row exists to record.",

    "ATTAINABLE CEILING: mechanically preventable over the standing enrolled population, not structurally guaranteed. Whether a claim's measured CPU, times the named runner envelope, crosses the ceiling is a measurement, not a source property; the invalid state stays writable and safety depends on the gate executing. Claiming structural impossibility would be inflation about an undecidable-from-source cost. The same ceiling the module already claims for new identities, applied to already-enrolled ones, is the honest climb -- still rung 2, over the population the purpose actually named.",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, naming the CAPABILITY: a wall that refuses an ALREADY-ENROLLED required identity whose measured CPU, multiplied by the named runner-inflation envelope, crosses the claim CPU ceiling -- the same `implied_clean_run_budget` derivation, over the standing declared population rather than declared-now minus declared-at-base. Sufficient that a row which degrades into the 450ms-then-coin-flip state after enrolment is refused on a later PR, not only on the PR that first enrolled it. A trigger that names only this increment gate, or that names a larger ceiling, does not discharge this: the first leaves the standing population unguarded, and the second papers over the cliff the module was written to refuse.)",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.workflow.floor_enrolment_margin", decl_name: "enrolment_margin_blockers", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.workflow.floor_enrolment_margin", decl_name: "floor_enrolment_margin_envelope_permille", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.workflow.floor_enrolment_margin", decl_name: "floor_enrolment_margin_budget_ms", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.workflow.floor_diff_observe", decl_name: "floor_run_base_test_decl_census", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.affected_set_universe", decl_name: "affected_set_universe_gate_processes_match_declared_gates", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.check_subject_narrower_than_its_declared_claim", decl_name: "check_subject_narrower_than_its_declared_claim", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
